{"type":"message","id":"2875845e","parentId":"86581654","timestamp":"2026-10-16T19:16:58.966Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass, including `test_dates`.\n\n**Cause:** the fixed format `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` had nothing to match the trailing `Z` (the UTC marker), so `strptime` stopped with \"unconverted data remains: Z\".\n\n**Fix:** the function now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead. On Python 3.11 and later, which covers the 3.13.5 installed here, it accepts a trailing `Z` and still handles timestamps without one.\n\n**Behaviour changes to be aware of:**\n- **Timezone-aware results:** a timestamp ending in `Z` or `+HH:MM` now comes back with UTC or that offset attached. Timestamps without one still come back as before, with no timezone. Code that compares the two kinds directly will raise a `TypeError`.\n- **Looser input:** it now accepts other ISO-8601 forms, such as a date alone (`\"2026-10-12\"`) or fractional seconds. The old version rejected these.\n- **Python version:** on Python older than 3.11, `fromisoformat` rejects `Z`. You'd need to replace the trailing `Z` with `+00:00` before parsing."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":438,"cacheRead":25571,"cacheWrite":1210,"totalTokens":27221,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":1210}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792178212631,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg6TEh7khb6wUdzzzJdXE","duration":6333.593990999998,"ttft":6300.041656999998,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26783,"nonMessageTokens":21646,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
